From 3f9b2f9347c11f78709967ad4c4818b9fe723c4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BullyMaguire-lol <temp9040@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:52:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] um: arm64: add a vDSO with clock_gettime() that does
 not trap

Every clock_gettime() and gettimeofday() of Android trapped into UML
(about 3 us on a phone). Map a real vDSO (AT_SYSINFO_EHDR) and a read-only
vvar page into every process instead:

- The vvar page holds the guest timekeeper's parameters (cycle_last,
  mult, shift, base, xtime_nsec of tkr_mono and tkr_raw, and the
  real/boot/tai offsets), updated from the pvclock_gtod notifier on every
  timekeeping update under a sequence count.
- The vDSO reads the host CLOCK_MONOTONIC through
  stub_vdso_clock_gettime() in the stub code page; the stub's seccomp
  filter now allows clock_gettime from there. It converts the host
  nanoseconds into "timer" clocksource cycles and applies exactly the
  timekeeper's formula, so results match the clock_gettime syscall (no
  steps backwards between the two).
- Other clocks, time travel mode, another clocksource and "novdsoclock"
  fall back to the system call. __kernel_rt_sigreturn moves from the
  signal trampoline page into the vDSO.

clock_gettime: 3.0 us -> 0.34 us.
